From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] grt: back the routing grid with a file in OBJECTS_DIR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

global_route needs more memory than many machines have on a large
design, and without swap set up for it the stage fails hours in.
global_route -backing_file reserves a file for the routing grid when the
grid is set up, failing at once when the disk cannot hold it, and the
kernel pages the grid to that file instead of to swap. The routes are
the same; the file is removed as soon as it is created.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an ORFS that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 flow/scripts/global_route.tcl | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl b/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl
index 35bd53e8..1de13dc0 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl
@@ -28,7 +28,9 @@ proc set_grt_seed { } {
 }
 
 proc run_global_route_and_catch_failures { args } {
-  if { [catch { log_cmd global_route {*}$args } errMsg] } {
+  if { [catch {
+    log_cmd global_route -backing_file $::env(OBJECTS_DIR)/grt.grid {*}$args
+  } errMsg] } {
     log_cmd write_db $::env(RESULTS_DIR)/5_1_grt-failed.odb
     error $errMsg
   }
@@ -91,7 +93,8 @@ if { !$::env(SKIP_INCREMENTAL_REPAIR) } {
 
   # Running DPL to fix overlapped instances
   # Run to get modified net by DPL
-  log_cmd global_route -start_incremental {*}$allow_congestion
+  log_cmd global_route -start_incremental {*}$allow_congestion \
+    -backing_file $::env(OBJECTS_DIR)/grt.grid
   detailed_placement_helper -quiet
   # Route only the modified net by DPL
   run_global_route_and_catch_failures -end_incremental {*}$res_aware \
@@ -108,7 +111,8 @@ if { !$::env(SKIP_INCREMENTAL_REPAIR) } {
     report_metrics 5 "global route post repair timing"
   }
 
-  log_cmd global_route -start_incremental {*}$allow_congestion
+  log_cmd global_route -start_incremental {*}$allow_congestion \
+    -backing_file $::env(OBJECTS_DIR)/grt.grid
   detailed_placement_helper -quiet
   log_cmd check_placement -placeable -verbose
   # Route only the modified net by DPL
@@ -136,7 +140,8 @@ if { !$::env(SKIP_INCREMENTAL_REPAIR) } {
 }
 
 if { !$::env(OPT_POST_GRT_WNS) } {
-  log_cmd global_route -start_incremental {*}$allow_congestion
+  log_cmd global_route -start_incremental {*}$allow_congestion \
+    -backing_file $::env(OBJECTS_DIR)/grt.grid
   recover_power_helper
   # Route the modified nets by rsz journal restore
   run_global_route_and_catch_failures -end_incremental {*}$res_aware \
